#       SV-258035 usbguard, SV-258081 policycoreutils
#       SV-258082 policycoreutils-python-utils, SV-258083 sudo
#       SV-258089 fapolicy, SV-258124 pcsc-lite, SV-258126 opensc
#       SV-258134 aide, SV-258140 rsyslog, SV-258151 audit
#       SV-258175 audispd-plugins, SV-258234 crypto-policies
#       SV-272488 postfix

META
    esp_id `ksi-svc-vri-cna-ibp-r9-required-packages-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `rocky9`
    criticality `high`

    title `KSI-SVC-VRI / KSI-CNA-IBP: Rocky 9 Required Security Packages`
    description `Validates that required security packages are installed including audit, AIDE, firewalld, chrony, sudo, fapolicy, PKI tools, and cryptographic policy management`
    author `scanset-security`
    tags `rocky9,stig,packages,security-tools,fedramp,KSI-SVC-VRI,KSI-CNA-IBP`

    control_mapping `KSI:KSI-SVC-VRI,KSI:KSI-CNA-IBP`
    control_objective `KSI-SVC-VRI,KSI-CNA-IBP`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Rocky9:localhost:package-management`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `1`
    recommendation `Install all missing packages via dnf install. These packages provide foundational security services required for FedRAMP compliance.`

    component_id `comp-r9-packages`

    impl_KSI_SVC_VRI `Service and resource integrity is validated by confirming the security toolchain is fully installed. AIDE provides file integrity monitoring. The audit package and audispd-plugins provide the audit subsystem. rsyslog provides log management. firewalld provides host firewall enforcement. chrony provides authenticated time synchronization. The crypto-policies package manages system-wide cryptographic policy. These packages collectively provide the monitoring, logging, and integrity verification capabilities required to detect unauthorized modifications.`

    impl_KSI_CNA_IBP `Isolation boundary protection tooling is validated by confirming policycoreutils and policycoreutils-python-utils are installed to manage SELinux policy, fapolicy is installed to enforce application whitelisting, usbguard is installed to control peripheral access, and openssh is installed to enforce encrypted remote access. PKI tools (openssl-pkcs11, gnutls-utils, nss-tools, pcsc-lite, opensc) support smart card and certificate-based authentication enforcement.`

META_END

